completed_at: "2026-10-15T06:09:34.666Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: Reproduce claimed release warning and current status contracts; Evaluate existing custom status/workflow primitives before adding baseline states; Design explicit history-backed handoff and verifier context without marking inactive work in progress; Cover context selection and close/reopen semantics
parent: pm-dj98
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "Project-defined evidence-backed handoff is atomic across SDK CLI and MCP, obeys workflow and ownership policies, and preserves compact receipts. Concise release help fits the existing512-byte command ceiling; compact help is328 bytes with an82-token cap."
expected_result: "Verification queues remain customizable and separate from active work, invalid handoffs preserve ownership/history, and progressive help stays within existing token-surface ceilings."
actual_result: "Current150 linked lifecycle tests and14 final flag/handoff checks pass. Initial hosted coverage100 percent in all four metrics, static and Windows checks passed. The failed552/512 help attempt is preserved; corrected509/512 help passes all58 surfaces without ceiling increases. Build, native contract/lexicon gates and packed Node/Bun acceptance pass. Require revised-head hosted checks/review before merge."
